### Task Model

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|----------------------|-------------------|
| **AT1: Calc Optimal Order** | Calculate optimal order of storages based on waiting time and path cost. | AND | Robot’s onboard planner | 1 | Only the robot performing the collection needs to compute the route. |
| **AT2: Nav & Req** | Navigate to storage and send request for resources. | AND | Storage location | 1 | Robot must physically reach the storage to request items. |
| **AT3: Wait Retrieval** | Wait until resources are retrieved from storage. | AND | Storage location | 1 | The robot must pause until the storage has handed over the items. |
| **AT4: Return Recharging** | Return to recharging station. | AND | Recharging station | 1 | Robot must recharge when battery < 10 %. |
| **AT5: Assign Collection** | Assign remaining collection tasks to another robot. | AND | Current location | 1 | Keeps the mission progressing after recharging. |
| **AT6: Nav to Delivery** | Navigate to delivery location carrying resources. | AND | Delivery location | 1 | Robot must reach the destination before delivery. |
| **AT7: Transport Resources** | Make necessary runs to transport all resources to the location. | AND | Delivery location | 1 | The robot may need multiple trips. |
| **AT8: Return to Checkpoint** | Return the resource to a checkpoint. | AND | Checkpoint | 1 | Safeguards the resource when battery < 30 %. |
| **AT9: Assign Delivery** | Assign remaining delivery tasks to another robot. | AND | Current location | 1 | Keeps the delivery going after checkpointing. |
| **AT10: Trigger Alert** | Trigger an alert. | AND | Robot’s communication module | 1 | Notify the system of the failure to return resource. |
| **AT11: Send Report** | Send report to sector manager. | AND | Sector manager | 1 | Inform human operator of the incident. |

